{"results": [{"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-063", "score": 0.125, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPA-063 | Study family SF-APPA-063: Holdout play-type rank validation (LAYER_AUDIT)\n- observed_research_question: Holdout play-type rank validation (LAYER_AUDIT)\n- auto_outcome_status: supported\n- observed_hypothesis: Pre-game PT PPP ranking from training data correlates with actual efficiency ranking in held-out games.\n- observed_result: Median rho +0.539 (IQR +0.245 to +0.750); 62.4% rho>0.4; 88.4% rho>0; 10.5% rho<0. Top-3 median hit 100%; >=2/3 hits 78.9%; median lift +0.4261 PPP; 90.8% positive lift. Bottom-3 median suppression 66.7%. MAE cited in la [cut; read_family for the full text]\n- auto_failure_mechanism: C_artifact (apparent effect produced by a construction, selection or labelling flaw)\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:DRIFT_NONSTATIONARITY\n- observed_failure_evidence: Doc caveat: top-3 lift partly reflects league-wide high-efficiency PTs (CUT, PUTBACK, TRANSITION); 10.5% of rows the model misleads (rho<0).\n- observed_sample_and_power: 908 game-team rows; 454 games\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF-APPA-035"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-034", "score": 0.108, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPA-034 | Study family SF-APPA-034: Opponent-relative leverage prevalence sweep\n- observed_research_question: Opponent-relative leverage prevalence sweep\n- auto_outcome_status: not a hypothesis test\n- observed_hypothesis: How often does an opponent-specific exploitable defensive weakness exist?\n- observed_result: Exploit available 33.3%; trap 23.3%; both 6.7%; neither 50.0%; median best edge 3.79%.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)\n- observed_failure_evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- observed_sample_and_power: 870 pairs\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- observed_method: 870 ordered team pairs; defense PT edge vs league >= +5% on seed PTs.\n- observed_verdict: descriptive\n- observed_failure_type: E_unclear\n- observed_notes: Edges depend only on the defense (e.g. DAL PNR +9.2% for every offense), so they are not matchup-specific.\n- auto_confidence: medium (0.65)\n- auto_addresses_question: RQC:RQC-010\n- auto_uses_dataset: DS:NCAA_tournament_and_ratings_data"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-066", "score": 0.105, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPA-066 | Study family SF-APPA-066: TOV_FORCE matchup decomposition on four playoff games\n- observed_research_question: TOV_FORCE matchup decomposition on four playoff games\n- auto_outcome_status: not a hypothesis test\n- observed_hypothesis: TOV_FORCE as a top-3 lever can be decomposed into defender x initiator x PT channels with positive matchup lift.\n- observed_result: Team-PT lifts are small (ORL vs DET PNR +1.2pp; POR vs SAS all PT lifts negative, e.g. PNR -4.1pp) while player-channel lifts are large on small n (Banchero on Huerter SPOT_UP +8.4pp, n_def=17 / n_off=54; Dort on Coffey  [cut; read_family for the full text]\n- auto_failure_mechanism: A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:insufficient_exposure\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:EXPOSURE_SPARSITY\n- observed_failure_evidence: Player-channel n often 15-28 defensive possessions; primary_defender attribution includes helper steals; no holdout or game-outcome check.\n- observed_sample_and_power: 4 games; cell n often 15-54"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPM-058", "score": 0.098, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPM-058 | Study family SF-APPM-058: PNR shot-level season rates vs possession labels\n- observed_research_question: PNR shot-level season rates vs possession labels\n- auto_outcome_status: not a hypothesis test\n- observed_hypothesis: PBP-derived shot-level PNR rates sit in a realistic band (script notes possession-level rates will be higher) and vary by team as expected.\n- observed_result: 2024-25 shot-level PNR share of half-court shots ranges from OKC 7.567% (498/6581) and BOS 7.854% to IND 13.824% (856/6192) and NYK 11.959%. ATL 11.361%, DEN 11.404%, PHX 10.232% (bh 7.050 / roll 3.181).\n- auto_failure_mechanism: E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)\n- observed_failure_evidence: No pass/fail gate in the output; rates are a calibration input for PBPProxyPNR (later logs show calibrated PNR ~17.9-19.6% of possessions).\n- observed_sample_and_power: 30 teams, half_court_shots ~5994-6581\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- observed_verdict: descriptive\n- observed_failure_type: E_unclear"}], "n_results": 4}

Stage 2. Using the retrieval result above (follow-up tools are allowed within the tool budget), complete steps 4 to 9
and reply with the final action. Output schema (all fields required):
